  "description": "The 2026 election for Kentucky's 2nd Congressional District pits 17-term Republican incumbent Brett Guthrie against Democratic nominee Megan Wingfield. Guthrie, who chairs the House Energy and Commerce Committee, has held the seat since 2009 and won re-election with 73.1% of the vote in 2024. The district, covering west-central Kentucky including Bowling Green, Owensboro, Elizabethtown, and part of eastern Louisville, is considered a safely Republican seat. Wingfield, a mechanic and first-time candidate, is running on a progressive platform emphasizing economic justice, healthcare access, and reproductive rights.",
